\description{
Maps paired-end reads from a single sample to a genome assembly
using BWA and then summarises read depth across contigs with mosdepth.
Reports per-contig mean and median depth and the proportion of bases covered
at 1x, 2x, 3x, 4x, 5x, 10x, and 20x thresholds. Results are written to a
CSV file in the output directory.

Simulates read-depth coverage across a range of sequencing
library sizes (in gigabases) by subsampling a real FASTQ dataset using
bbmap reformat.sh. For each simulated library size, reads are mapped to the
genome with BWA, depth is estimated with mosdepth over a random subset of
contigs, and coverage statistics (mean/median depth, proportion of bases at
1x-20x) are recorded. All results are written to a CSV file.

A second variant of the genome coverage simulator that sweeps a
finer-grained set of simulated library sizes (internally set to 1-10 GB in
1 GB steps) and additionally produces a coverage-versus-depth line plot
using ggplot2 after all subsampling is complete. Otherwise identical in
approach to \code{genomeCoverageSimulator}: reads are subsampled with
bbmap reformat.sh, mapped with BWA, and depth is assessed with mosdepth
over a random subset of contigs of length >= 500 bp.

Simulates sequencing coverage at multiple depths by subsampling
